@* The operating systems Fleeto supports and how far (0.8.0 step 4, VULNERABILITIES.md §12): the catalog SupportedProducts, kept in code with
   the features, so every operating system Fleeto adds appears here. *@
<div class="fl-panel">
    <MudSimpleTable Dense="true" Elevation="0" Hover="true">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Operating system</th>
                <th>Monitoring</th>
                <th>Patching</th>
                <th>Remote control</th>
                <th>Remote background</th>
                <th>Vulnerabilities</th>
                <th>Web interface</th>
                <th>End-of-life dates</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            @foreach (var product in SupportedProducts.All)
            {
                var info = EndOfLife.Info(product.Product);
                <tr>
                    <td>
                        <strong>@info.Name</strong>
                        <div class="muted">@product.Versions</div>
                    </td>
                    <td>@Cell(product.Monitoring)</td>
                    <td>@Cell(product.Patching)</td>
                    <td>@Cell(product.RemoteControl)</td>
                    <td>@Cell(product.RemoteBackground)</td>
                    <td>@Cell(product.Vulnerabilities)</td>
                    <td>@Cell(product.WebInterface)</td>
                    <td><MudLink Href="@info.SourceLink" Target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@info.SourceName</MudLink></td>
                </tr>
            }
        </tbody>
    </MudSimpleTable>
</div>
<MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Class="muted mt-2 d-block">
    Other operating systems can run the Fleeto agent where it supports them, but are not in the end-of-life report. Remote control needs Windows 10 or
    Server 2016 or newer, or Linux with a desktop on X11. macOS is not supported.
</MudText>

@code {
    private static RenderFragment Cell(FeatureSupport support) => support.Level switch
    {
        SupportLevel.Yes => @<span>
            <StatusChip Text="Yes" Kind="StatusKind.Ok" />
            @if (support.Note is { } note)
            {
                <div class="muted">@note</div>
            }
        </span>,
        SupportLevel.Partly => @<span>
            <StatusChip Text="Partly" Kind="StatusKind.Warning" />
            @if (support.Note is { } note)
            {
                <div class="muted">@note</div>
            }
        </span>,
        _ => @<span>
            <StatusChip Text="No" Kind="StatusKind.Neutral" />
            @if (support.Note is { } note)
            {
                <div class="muted">@note</div>
            }
        </span>
    };
}
